[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:16. A Polite Request]
[00:00.560]Passage 16 | 文章十六
[00:02.940]A polite request | 一个礼貌的请求
[00:06.090]If you park your car in the wrong place, | 如果你把车停错了地方，
[00:10.200]a traffic policeman will soon find it. | 交通警察很快就会发现它。
[00:13.525]You will be very lucky if he lets you go without a ticket. | 如果他让你不贴罚单就走，你就算非常幸运了。
[00:18.255]However, this does not always happen. | 然而，这并不总是发生。
[00:22.060]Traffic police are sometimes very polite. | 交通警察有时非常礼貌。
[00:25.325]During a holiday in Sweden, I found this note on my car. | 在瑞典度假期间，我在我的车上发现了这张纸条。
[00:30.225]Sir, we welcome you to our city. | 先生，我们欢迎您来到我们的城市。
[00:34.275]This is a no parking area. | 这里是禁止停车区。
[00:37.650]You will enjoy your stay here if you pay attention to our street signs. | 如果您留意我们的路标，您会在这里度过愉快的时光。
[00:43.580]This note is only a reminder. | 这张纸条只是一个提醒。
[00:47.550]If you receive a request like this, | 如果你收到这样的请求，
[00:51.150]you cannot fail to obey it. | 你就不能不遵守。